{
  "spec": "CONTROL.md §14.4 (a broken notice)",
  "note": "A broken notice whose `id` can be read is acked `refused` with `bad_notice`, so the receiver stops sending it; one whose `id` cannot be read has nothing to ack, and the machine drops it each time it comes (the receiver drops it when it expires). A broken notice never stops a message of the same poll answer or another notice. A poll answer with more than 50 notices is read for its first 50, in order; the rest stay unacked and come again. (In the second case card-todo's cap is 5 and the machine starts 2 at once: 2 run, 3 wait counted, and the rest are past the cap.)",
